<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41466" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτυμβ-ίδιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
			ʽτύμβοσ̓</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>at</i> or <i>over a tomb,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρῆνοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					342
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν δ᾽ ἐ. τούτῳ θῆκεν χάριν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1409.5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτυμβίδιοι κορυδαλλίδες</span>
			<i>frequenting tombs,</i> or <i>with tomb-like crests,</i> or
				<i>with tombs in their heads</i> (v.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				475
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				7.23
			</span></i>, cf. Sch.adloc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
